4. **PILOT's file family is PILOT-owned** — `.pilot/pilot.py`, `.pilot/pilot_checks.py`, `.pilot/formats.json`,
   `.pilot/workflows/`, the `.pilot/pilot-*.md` docs, every `.claude/skills/pilot-*/SKILL.md`, every
   `.claude/agents/pilot-*.md`, and the `PILOT:` marked blocks in this file and `README.md`. All of it is copied
   in from [github.com/Jonas-Eve/pilot](https://github.com/Jonas-Eve/pilot): never hand-edit any of it, run
   `/pilot-update` instead. A renamed label, moved section or changed workflow upstream can leave stale
   references in this file's or `README.md`'s own prose outside the marked blocks: after `/pilot-update`,
   `grep` the terms that changed and skim that prose against what changed.
5. **The project's own commands live in `.pilot/state.json`** (`commands`), set with
   `python3 .pilot/pilot.py config set commands.<key> "<command>"` (`test`, `rules`, `e2e`, `build`, `a11y`,
   `render`, `version`): the code checks of a workflow read their results. Exclude docs-only paths (`wiki/`,
   `architecture/`) from the project's CI; end-to-end tests never run in CI.
